@startuml
title Messenger - Simplified Data Flow Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 75
skinparam ArrowColor #40556B
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #E8F3FC
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #FFF5D6

rectangle "User\n(visitor or logged in)" as User

rectangle "Messenger" {
  together {
    usecase "P1\nAccounts and Sessions" as P1
    usecase "P2\nConversations and Groups" as P2
    usecase "P3\nMessages" as P3
  }
  database "D1 - Messenger Data\nAccounts and sessions\nConversations and members\nTemporary messages" as Data
}

User --> P1 : Registration, login, logout,\nor username lookup data
P1 --> User : Account / session /\nlookup result
Data --> P1 : Account and session records
P1 --> Data : New accounts (hashed passwords)\nand session changes

User --> P2 : Session, conversation details,\nmember changes, list query
P2 --> User : Conversation list /\nmanagement result
Data --> P2 : Users, sessions,\nconversations and members
P2 --> Data : New conversations /\nupdated membership

User --> P3 : Session, conversation ID,\nmessage text / read request
P3 --> User : Authorized messages /\naccess-denied result
Data --> P3 : Sessions, members,\nand current messages
P3 --> Data : Authorized new messages

legend bottom
  Rectangles: users / boundary. Ovals: processes. Cylinder: data store.
  Arrows show data, not execution order. User includes senders and recipients.
  P2/P3 check login and permissions. D1 combines logical data for readability.
  Sessions and messages are temporary. Other restart persistence: IA03 Q-04.
endlegend
@enduml
